   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 704 of the laws of 1991, amending the arts and cultural affairs law and chapter 912 of the laws of 1920 relating to the regulation of boxing and wrestling matches relating to tickets to places of entertainment; and chapter 151 of the laws of 2010, amending the arts and cultural affairs law relating to resale of tickets to places of entertainment, in relation to extending the effectiveness of the provisions thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6004",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6004-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §4, Chap 704 of 1991; amd §11, Chap 151 of 2010",
    "lawSection": "Arts and Cultural Affairs",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6004\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 704 of the laws of 1991,\namending the arts and cultural affairs law and chapter 912 of the laws\nof 1920 relating to the regulation of boxing and wrestling matches\nrelating to tickets to places of entertainment; and chapter 151 of the\nlaws of 2010, amending the arts and cultural affairs law relating to\nresale of tickets to places of entertainment, in relation to extending\nthe effectiveness of the provisions thereof\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill extends the existing statutes relating to places of\nentertainment and the resale of tickets.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 extends the present law on the resale of tickets until and\nincluding June 30, 2018.\n\nSection 2 extends the various provision of Arts and Cultural Law\narticle 25 through June 30, 2018.\n\nSection 3 states that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nIn the 2010 legislative session, significant changes were made to the\nlaw on the sale and resale of tickets to places of entertainment. As\nthe market evolves ensuring the protection of consumers and their\nrights becomes increasingly important. This legislation allows for\nadditional time to fully understand the effects these regulatory\nchances and new technologies will have on industry and consumers alike\nby extending the current provisions until and including June 30, 2018.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2016: S7181/A9773 - Chapter 34 of the laws of 2016\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
